1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,371
Lyman: Get out of my potatoes!

2
00:00:01,691 --> 00:00:07,174
Telegraph: Post Time Lowpoly. The Pig War.
Part one of three: one pig.

3
00:00:07,494 --> 00:00:12,170
Telegraph: Eighteen fifty-nine. One
farmer. One big pig.

4
00:00:12,490 --> 00:00:14,601
Lyman: It ate my whole potato patch.

5
00:00:14,921 --> 00:00:15,960
Lyman: So I shot it.

6
00:00:16,521 --> 00:00:17,523
Griffin: That was MY pig!

7
00:00:18,121 --> 00:00:20,096
Lyman: Ten dollars. Final offer.

8
00:00:20,216 --> 00:00:20,898
Griffin: One hundred.

9
00:00:21,218 --> 00:00:22,247
Lyman: Then arrest me.

10
00:00:22,818 --> 00:00:24,996
Griffin: Oh, I will. Britain owns this
island.

11
00:00:25,116 --> 00:00:26,258
Lyman: America owns it.

12
00:00:26,578 --> 00:00:28,609
Pickett: Sixty-six soldiers. Landing now.

13
00:00:28,929 --> 00:00:32,756
Telegraph: One pig. Zero survivors.
Hundreds of soldiers.

14
00:00:33,076 --> 00:00:36,467
Telegraph: What is the silliest reason you
know of for a fight? Tell me below.

15
00:00:36,787 --> 00:00:43,739
Telegraph: Part one of three, The Pig War.
Next dispatch: the standoff. Follow for part two.

